+
+### 7.1 R1 controlled caller authentication, trusted delegation and official-document view — T11DR-01
+
+Selected controlled authentication has two independent checks on **every provider route**, including discovery, assertion issuance, publish, exact execution/result lookup and document content: (a) `Authorization: Bearer <256-bit random service secret>` identifies the explicitly installed application client; (b) bounded Ed25519-signed `X-Controlled-Delegation` identifies the server-authorized actor, purpose and exact resource. Missing/wrong bearer is401 before routing protected data or effects; authenticated caller with invalid delegation/purpose/resource/actor is403. TLS authenticates the configured server; it does not replace either client check. The secret and signing material never come from browser JSON/headers forwarded wholesale, model config or provider-supplied URLs.
+
+Root creates the secret and application delegation signing key once per explicit controlled fixture run; across app/provider process restarts the same run reloads the same restricted credential files (POSIX0600 or equivalent Windows owner/service-only ACL). They are outside repository/archive/evidence/log paths; application receives only its client secret/private key, provider receives a verifier hash for the bearer and the exact application public key/clientId. No secret in CLI arguments, screenshots, URLs, audit, canonical semantic digest, stored request_manifest or publication_submission. Credential rotation is explicit coordinated fixture administration, not per-process regeneration or automatic trust-on-first-use; old immutable request/result histories retain clientId/store identity, never a credential. This is local controlled client trust, not company login or hostile-host qualification.
+
+Provider durable store pins providerId, random storeInstanceId, clientId, allowed delegation public key/keyId, provider assertion-signing public key/keyId and current grant records. Application configuration pins the same provider/store/assertion key and TLS origin; replacing the SQLite file or key behind an unchanged endpoint fails identity validation, not a new empty store. Provider assertion private key lives in its restricted fixture credential store, never in application. Delegation/assertion signature input is exact bounded canonical JSON with explicit schema/domain separation; Ed25519, no algorithm negotiation. Maximum header4KiB, signature64bytes/base64url canonical; issue/expiry whole UTC seconds, expiry≤issued+30s, bounded clock skew2s, expired/future/malformed/duplicate claims reject. No signature parsing or keys below browser control.
+
+Delegation claims: `{schema:"ama.controlled-kb-delegation.v1",issuer:clientId,keyId,audience:providerId,storeInstanceId,actorId,purpose,method,resource,issuedAt,expiresAt,nonce,requestDigest}`. ActorId is selected from an authenticated application session after genuine B03 gate, or from the immutable submission.requester_id for a background operation, never the caller's claimed actor. A constructor-private adapter `AuthorizedKnowledgeCall` is minted only by the registered service/worker bridge after fresh gate verification; no public signer or arbitrary actor method. For initial publish the current genuine owner must equal that stored original requester, exact accepted task/request/final/r/e must remain valid, and Task7 initial-send admission is still required. The request actorId must byte-match delegation and destination assertion; mismatches deny before document/slot mutation. Owner transfer is still unsupported, not silently reattributed.
+
+Purposes are finite: DESTINATION_READ (actor's current library/folder discovery), DESTINATION_AUTHORIZE (exact destination), PUBLISH (exact publication/submission task/execution/key/destination/request digests), RECEIPT_LOOKUP (exact original client-owned publication/execution/key/result), DOCUMENT_READ (current viewer plus actual immutable document/destination). `resource` is canonical fixed IDs, not arbitrary URL. `requestDigest` covers exact canonical body for POST or canonical route/query IDs for GET, excluding bearer/delegation/signature fields; it is transport verification, not the durable command semantic digest. A public request cannot choose another purpose or get a signed broader resource. Signed claims expire; replaying an exact PUBLISH within that lifetime still hits immutable execution/provider-slot idempotency and cannot authorize another effect.
+
+Destination assertion issuance authenticates client+delegation before looking up actor grants and refuses arbitrary actor claims. The returned signed assertion binds schema/providerId/storeInstanceId/audience clientId/actorId/exact library+folder/authVersion/issuedAt/expiresAt and the requested publication/submission context where applicable. Adapter pins verifier to configured store/key; provider rechecks signature, full context, current authVersion/grant and live PUBLISH delegation before effect. Assertion possession without caller credentials/current matching delegation grants nothing. Assertions remain transient; no secret or signed token enters persistence/digests/browser.
+
+Receipt reconciliation must outlive revocation without restoring business permission: RECEIPT_LOOKUP is a service-client capability limited to the original accepted submission identity and exact immutable result/execution owned by that client, even if its original actor is now disabled or lacks destination rights. Application mints it only from the registered durable execution/submission recovery path; a browser cannot request arbitrary lookup. Provider verifies stored client/actor/request ownership and returns bounded receipt facts, not document content or another client's records. If the exact execution has not been observed in this pinned store, a valid narrowly scoped service delegation may receive only bounded UNKNOWN/NOT_OBSERVED; absence grants no provider-zero-effect proof, binding replacement, document data or new send. A present record with mismatched ownership denies instead of disclosing it. Task7 still decides current application versus fact-only. Interactive owner status requires fresh meeting ACL; member gets the sanitized projection. DESTINATION_* and DOCUMENT_READ instead require the actor/viewer's current provider grants; receipt permission never substitutes.
+
+**Official document path stays usable:** add authenticated same-origin `GET /api/v1/meetings/{meetingId}/publications/{publicationId}/document` and return that path as `officialDocumentUrl` in browser projections. Browser uses its real app session; no provider bearer/delegation/assertion in URL, cookie, DOM, screenshots or redirect. Server S phase authenticates fresh meeting READ, exact immutable publication mapping/provider/document/final and allowed lifecycle. Outside locks it calls fixed `GET /v1/knowledge/documents/{documentId}` using service credentials plus fresh DOCUMENT_READ delegation for the actual viewer. Provider verifies the document's actual library/folder and current viewer READ grant before returning its immutable bounded payload, denying401/403 without content. Server F rechecks fresh meeting authorization/mapping/lifecycle before emitting buffered bounded content, never holds DB roots over transport. Thus app READ alone and provider READ alone each are insufficient. Configure actual owner/member provider READ grants in the controlled successful fixture; denied member/outsider/admin proves both checks independently.
+
+The provider has no unauthenticated browser document portal or share token. Its internal stored document_url remains validated metadata; application never redirects browser there. Relay renders exact provider immutable document payload as escaped text/HTML with static template, `Cache-Control: private,no-store`, `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'`, `X-Content-Type-Options:nosniff`, no active raw HTML/Markdown/resources. Whole response shares8MiB payload and32MiB encoded limits, same watchdog/cancellation, no arbitrary URL fetch. App fresh meeting ACL and provider grant are point-in-time authorizations; no long-lived access capability is exported. Revocation/withdrawal/obsolescence denies subsequent reads through existing lifecycle rules.
+
+Actual HTTP evidence gate: missing/wrong bearer on every route; valid bearer but absent/expired/bad-signature/wrong audience/store/client/actor/purpose/method/resource/digest delegation; body actor differing from delegated actor; stolen destination assertion with different actor/request; provider-store replacement/key mismatch; caller requests another client's result; revoked actor still permits only exact registered service RECEIPT_LOOKUP and no publish/document. Assert no assertion/data/slot/document effect or unauthorized read on negatives. Positive real-browser official view uses relay for owner/member with BOTH grants; separately revoke meeting READ and provider READ, test outsider/role-only admin/direct provider URL denial and no credential exposure. These are future tests, not executions in this repair.
