+### 8.5 R1 genuine never-marked local terminal failure, durable acceptance and explicit recovery — T11DR-02
+
+**Actual gap, not an existing feature.** JdbcTaskQueue.claimOne at original line108 fails exhausted tasks; completeValidated at136–143 turns exhausted RETRYABLE into FAILED. terminateUnmarkedExecution145–151 does nothing when initial task has no execution and, for PREPARED, only changes external rows to FAILED/LOCAL_PREPARED_ATTEMPT_LIMIT. Neither writes publication. Worker ordinary failure/quarantine can likewise leave task terminal or RECONCILING without a marker. Publication READY cannot remain an irreversible freeze for this provably local case. Also V013 publication current fields are mutable, task input is only PUBLICATION:id/fingerprint and idempotency_record stores only result_id/hash: after a no-execution failure and destination/final change there is **no existing immutable accepted header**. Hashes cannot reconstruct that header. R1 requires the following minimal prospective metadata model; absent it the new flow is unavailable, never backfilled or faked.
+
+**Prospective `publication_submission` logical shape (no SQL/migration number allocated):**
+
+| Column | Exact proposed storage/meaning |
+|---|---|
+| task_id | char(36) ASCII binary, NOT NULL, PK, FK durable_task(id); actual accepted task, no invented execution. |
+| publication_id | char(36) ASCII binary NOT NULL, FK publication(id). |
+| submission_no | bigint unsigned NOT NULL; positive monotonically allocated per publication, supported≤9223372036854775806; UNIQUE(publication_id,submission_no). |
+| confirmation_id | char(36) ASCII binary NOT NULL, FK final_confirmation(id); exact accepted final, immutable. |
+| provider_id | varchar(64) ASCII binary NOT NULL; configured provider code. |
+| business_key | varchar(255) utf8mb4_0900_bin NOT NULL; exact publicationId:confirmationId. Not globally unique here because several submissions can use one key. |
+| library_id, folder_id | each varchar(255) utf8mb4_0900_bin NOT NULL; exact accepted real destination IDs. |
+| requester_id | varchar(255) utf8mb4_0900_bin NOT NULL, FK enterprise_identity(enterprise_id); original authenticated owner, immutable. |
+| logical_request_hash, execution_request_hash | each char(64) ASCII binary NOT NULL; lowercase canonical SHA256. |
+| request_manifest | LONGTEXT NOT NULL; strict bounded content-free original acceptance manifest schema, maximum64KiB UTF8/64Ki UTF16. Contains original render identity/payload hash/provider-store identity/clientId/submission_no/taskId/expected execution number/r/e and immutable predecessor reference plan; no document text or credentials/delegations/assertions. |
+| created_at | datetime(6) NOT NULL; real accepted DB time. |
+| local_state | varchar(32) ASCII binary NOT NULL, `UNDECIDED` or `NEVER_MARKED`; no provider outcome implied. |
+| local_decided_at | datetime(6) nullable; actual atomic local terminal decision time. |
+| local_reason | varchar(64) ASCII binary nullable; allowlisted PREPARATION_EXHAUSTED, TERMINAL_UNMARKED_FAILURE or EXPIRED_UNMARKED_ABANDONED. |
+| local_decided_by | varchar(255) utf8mb4_0900_bin nullable, FK enterprise_identity; fresh authorizing owner, not a claim that background recovery was a human click. Audit separately records actual worker/command initiator. |
+| local_attempt_no | bigint unsigned nullable; exact actual last queue attempt observed at decision (0 allowed if no attempt ever started). |
+| local_execution_id | char(36) ASCII binary nullable, FK external_execution(id); actual unmarked PREPARED/locally failed execution when one exists; null only for genuinely no execution. |
+
+All FKs RESTRICT update/delete. Additional index `(local_state,created_at,task_id)` supports bounded local-recovery enumeration; UNIQUE(publication_id,submission_no) supplies complete publication membership. CHECK submission_no>0, local_state vocabulary; UNDECIDED means all local_* fields after local_state NULL; NEVER_MARKED means time/reason/actor/attempt nonnull with exact reason vocabulary (execution may be null). Runtime validates SHA/UUID/manifest bytes, task subject/type/input/fingerprint/r/e/producer, original final/destination/provider and execution association; SQL FK alone does not prove same meeting. Immutable binding columns NEVER update. Only one atomic UNDECIDED→NEVER_MARKED change with affected-count1 is permitted, filling all decision columns; replay requires exact same sealed decision and never changes time/reason/actor/attempt. No reset/overwrite/decision from provider errors.
+
